/A 2141 0 R
/Alt (The scatter plot titled Partition of the symbolic space displays a bifurcation diagram. The horizontal axis is labelled u, ranging from 0.6 to 2.0. The vertical axis is labelled xn, ranging from minus 1.00 to 1.00. A dashed horizontal line is present at xn equals 0.00. The plot shows two distinct regions. The upper region, labelled R Composite area, consists of blue points and generally occupies xn values greater than 0.00. It starts around u equals 0.55 with xn around 0.75, then bifurcates multiple times, showing complex patterns of points that spread out and then narrow. The lower region, labelled L Prime area, consists of red points and generally occupies xn values less than 0.00. It mirrors the upper region, starting around u equals 1.0 with xn around 0.00, then bifurcating and spreading out into complex patterns of points that narrow again towards u equals 2.0. Both regions show period doubling bifurcations as u increases, leading to chaotic behaviour.)
/K 40
/P 39 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
