/Alt (The line graph displays Lyapunov Exponent Estimation with embedding m equals 6. The horizontal axis represents Evolution Steps k, ranging from 0 to 50. The vertical axis represents Log Divergence ln absolute value of dj k, ranging from minus 8 to 0. Three data series are plotted: Primes Data, Logistic Data, and Random Noise. The Primes Data series, represented by a line with circular markers, starts near minus 0.5 at k equals 0, rises to approximately 0.5 by k equals 5, then plateaus at about 0.5 from k equals 5 to 50. The Logistic Data series, represented by a line with circular markers, starts near minus 7.8 at k equals 0, increases steadily to approximately minus 0.5 by k equals 25, then plateaus at about minus 0.5 from k equals 25 to 50. The Random Noise series, represented by a dashed line, starts near minus 0.5 at k equals 0, rises sharply to approximately 0.5 by k equals 2, then plateaus at about 0.5 from k equals 2 to 50. Two fit lines are also shown: Primes Fit with MLE equals 0.098, which is a straight line segment from k equals 0 to approximately k equals 15, and Logistic Fit with MLE equals 0.337, which is a straight line segment from k equals 0 to approximately k equals 15.)
/K 13
/P 39 0 R
/Pg 27 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
