/A 2428 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel line graph shows block entropy and entropy rate for prime and logistic sequences versus block size k. Panel a, titled Block Entropy H\(k\), has a horizontal axis labelled Block Size k from 0 to 12 and a vertical axis labelled Entropy in bits from 0 to 12. The Primes Renormalized line, marked with blue circles, increases linearly from approximately 1 bit at k equals 1 to 11.5 bits at k equals 12. The Logistic u equals 1.5437 line, marked with red squares, increases linearly from approximately 1 bit at k equals 1 to 10.5 bits at k equals 12. Both lines run below the Pure Random H equals k dashed grey line, which increases from 0 to 12. Panel b, titled Entropy Rate h\(k\) equals H\(k plus 1\) minus H\(k\), has a horizontal axis labelled Block Size k from 0 to 12 and a vertical axis labelled Entropy Rate in bits per symbol from 0.0 to 1.0. The Primes Entropy Rate line, marked with blue circles, starts at approximately 0.95 bits per symbol at k equals 1, remains relatively flat until k equals 10, then slightly decreases to approximately 0.9 bits per symbol at k equals 12. The Logistic Entropy Rate line, marked with red squares, starts at approximately 0.88 bits per symbol at k equals 1, remains relatively flat until k equals 10, then slightly decreases to approximately 0.85 bits per symbol at k equals 12. Both lines are above the 0.)
/K 15
/P 39 0 R
/Pg 27 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
