/Alt (The line graph shows quantitative verification of Twin Prime Constant. The horizontal axis is labelled Evolution Steps n, ranging from 0.0 to 1.0 times 10 to the power of 7. The vertical axis is labelled Estimated Constant C, ranging from 0.650 to 0.800. A dashed line labelled Simple Method \(Biased\) starts at approximately 0.800 and gradually decreases to approximately 0.765 across the horizontal axis. A solid line labelled Integral Method \(Corrected\) starts at approximately 0.650, increases to approximately 0.660, then stabilises around 0.660 across the horizontal axis. A dashed line labelled Hardy-Littlewood C2 is constant at approximately 0.660 across the entire horizontal axis, with a label 0.65984 at its right end. An inset titled Zoom: 40 percentage - 95 percentage Iterations shows a magnified view of the Integral Method \(Corrected\) line and the Hardy-Littlewood C2 line. The inset horizontal axis ranges from 4 to 9 times 10 to the power of 6. The inset vertical axis ranges from 0.65950 to 0.66075. In the inset, the Integral Method \(Corrected\) line fluctuates around the Hardy-Littlewood C2 line, which is constant at approximately 0.66000.)
