/A 2480 0 R
/Alt (The graph titled Microscopic Statistics: Cramer Conjecture Test displays Probability Density P\(g\) on the vertical axis, ranging from 10 to the power of 0 to 10 to the power of minus 4 on a logarithmic scale, against Normalised Gap g over g bar on the horizontal axis, ranging from 0 to 6. Four data series are plotted. The Cramer Conjecture, represented by a red dashed line, shows a steady exponential decay from approximately 10 to the power of 0 at a normalised gap of 0, decreasing to about 10 to the power of minus 3 at a normalised gap of 6. The Aging Model, a green solid line, closely follows the Cramer Conjecture curve, starting near 10 to the power of 0 and decaying similarly. Real Primes, a blue solid line, also closely tracks the Cramer Conjecture and Aging Model, showing a similar decay pattern. The Static Model, a grey dotted line, deviates significantly, exhibiting a more erratic, stepped pattern that is generally higher than the other curves at lower normalised gaps and then drops below them at higher normalised gaps.)
